.env
*.local
/bsystem-integration-core/
/bsystem-hub/
/bsystem-design-system/

# Editor and OS noise. Listed once here rather than in each contributor's
# global config, so a stray file cannot reach a review.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Where `go build` writes when nobody passes -o: a main package at a module
# root builds to a file named after the directory, one under cmd/ to a file
# named after the command. bsystem-integration-core committed a 13 MB binary
# through exactly this gap. scripts/check-artifacts.py keeps this list in step
# with the modules rather than waiting for somebody to notice again.
loadtest/loadtest
mocks/mock-espocrm
mocks/mock-identity
mocks/mock-outline
mocks/mock-redmine

# Python bytecode. scripts/ is full of Python that CI and contributors run, and
# importing any of it as a module leaves a .pyc behind. Nothing covered it, and
# check-artifacts.py could not have caught a committed one either: its magic
# table knew ELF, MZ, Mach-O, zip, gzip, xz and zstd, but not bytecode. Both
# halves of that gap are closed together — ignoring it here, and refusing a
# tracked one there.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
